eria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1775,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'That endpoint is HTTPS and behind the OAuth gate (REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL / REBAR_MCP_AUTH_ISSUER_URL …), so an unauthenticated call satisfies nothing … The validating client MUST present the OAuth bearer token that docs/mcp-client-setup.md configures'","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:363 — REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STRATEGIES: \"static\"","docs/mcp-client-setup.md:8 — 'None of the three requires OAuth for this deployment — one static-bearer shape covers all three.'","docs/mcp-auth.md §7 — 'authenticated by the static verifier with one bearer PAT per client (Copilot, Codex, Claude). No Authorization Server is stood up … none require OAuth/DCR'","docs/mcp-client-setup.md — the token is the per-client PAT env var MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT, presented as 'Authorization: Bearer <PAT>' by the static verifier"],"finding":"The LIVE VALIDATION 'Auth precondition' mischaracterizes the deployed endpoint's auth as an OAuth gate requiring an 'OAuth bearer token', but the deployed server authenticates with a STATIC bearer PAT (auth_strategies='static'), not OAuth.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f89fde926100f7b14","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria → LIVE VALIDATION → 'Auth precondition' paragraph","norm_id":"nca8b21daf4687da1","priority":0.7225,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A validator obtains an OAuth token via a code/token flow (per the plan) and finds no such flow, blocking the LIVE VALIDATION close","A validator interprets the static PAT it must use as 'not the OAuth token the plan demands' and reports the precondition unmet"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Rewrite the precondition to: the /mcp endpoint is HTTPS behind the in-app STATIC bearer verifier (REBAR_MCP_AUTH_STRATEGIES=static); the validating client MUST present its static PAT as 'Authorization: Bearer <MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT>' per docs/mcp-client-setup.md. REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL/ISSUER_URL are the RS audience / PRM metadata, not a client OAuth flow. A 401/403 is still a FAILED validation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.85,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Remove or correct the 'fronted by infra/terraform/auth/edge-gate' citation; edge-gate is an un-deployed browser SSO cookie gate, not the MCP endpoint's auth — name the in-app static verifier (docker-compose.yml) instead.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1775,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'behind the OAuth gate (… fronted by infra/terraform/auth/edge-gate)'","infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md:3 — 'Google-OAuth SSO gate for *.solutions.navateam.com … mints a domain-wide, HMAC-signed session cookie; each protected CloudFront distribution runs a viewer-request Lambda@Edge (the sso-gate module)'","infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md:63-64 — 'rebar currently runs no gate instance — the auth host + module are staged f